# Design

Read `docs/DESIGN.md` before changing anything visual. Encode every number in
`src/lib/design.ts` in the same change. Markdown that is not a token is a rule
nobody follows.

## Never

- A literal hex value, `fontSize`, `fontFamily`, `letterSpacing`, or raw pixel
  gap in a component. Everything comes from `src/lib/design.ts`.
- `StyleSheet.create` at module scope with colours in it. Colours change when the
  scheme flips, so styles come from `useThemedStyles(factory)`.
- A named font family, a bundled font, or a `useFonts` call. The type is SF
  Pro, which is the system face: `family` is `undefined` on native and a stack
  on web, and both arrive through `type`.
- A weight outside `weight` — no 300, no 500, no `fontWeight` written inline.
- `textTransform: 'uppercase'`, or a string literal written in caps. Copy we
  write is sentence case; only proper nouns take a capital. Dealer data
  (brand, model, reference) is printed as imported and never re-cased.
- A glyph from outside `MaterialCommunityIcons`, or a hand-picked size for one.
  Outline when idle, solid when active, `size.icon` or `size.iconSmall`.
- An icon-only control without an `accessibilityLabel` naming what it does.
- `save` or `danger` colour used for anything but saving and passing.
- A capsule radius. Controls use `radius.sm`, fields and tiles use `md`, and the
  swipe card uses `lg`. There is no `pill` token to reach for.
- `contentFit="contain"` on a photo frame. A browsing frame — card, tile,
  thumbnail, detail hero — fills with `cover`. Only the full-screen viewer keeps
  the whole photograph.
- `borderWidth` on four sides of anything at all. Nothing in this app is drawn
  with an outline: a card, tile, panel, or notice is a `surface` fill, a control
  with a label is a `fill`, and a container inside a container takes
  `surfaceSunken`. A hairline on *one* edge is a separator and is fine — `border`
  for those, `size.rule` for a chosen row's brass mark.
- Any background behind an icon-only control. The glyph is the control; it gets
  a `HIT_TARGET` box of empty space and colour for state, never a block.
- A shadow or elevation in place of the outline you just removed. Depth is the
  colour step between `background`, `surface`, `fill`, and `surfaceSunken`.
- A ring, outline, or second fill a shade away to show state. Selection is
  `brass`: as a fill with a `background` label, or as the glyph colour.
- `surfaceSunken` on something sitting directly on the page. It is darker than
  the page in the dark scheme and disappears there; it only works inside a
  container.
- A badge around data. A box around a name makes it look like a control, so a
  dealer's name on a card is type and colour, not a box.
- Type laid straight on a photograph. It goes in `PhotoCaption`, on `scrim`.
  Half the watches are shot on white and white type vanishes on them.
- The year in a specification line. It belongs to the name — `formatModel`
  gives "Datejust, 1968", `formatSpecs` gives what the name did not say.
- A filled button except the final `Send inquiry` action. `Button` defaults to
  fill; callers request `solid` explicitly.
- `Dimensions.get('window')` at module scope. It never updates on a browser
  resize. Use `useWindowDimensions` for the viewport, `onLayout` for an element.
- A screen, card, or text column with no maximum width. Widths come from
  `layout`; `Screen` applies one by default.
- `Platform.OS` used to ask how much room there is. That is a width question,
  so branch on width. Reserve `Platform.OS` for capability.
- `showsVerticalScrollIndicator={false}` to quiet a scrollbar. Web scrollbars
  are already styled down in `applyScrollbarStyle`; hiding one per scroll view
  removes the reader's only sense of how much is left.
- A hardcoded number for a notch, Dynamic Island, or home indicator. Insets
  come from `react-native-safe-area-context`.
- A guess at where a navigator put something. The save flight measures the
  Saved bookmark with `measureInWindow` rather than dividing the window by the
  tab count, and degrades to no animation until that measurement arrives.
- A `tabBar*` styling option in the tabs layout. The bar is `TabBar`; the
  layout declares routes, titles, icons, and `tabBarPosition`, nothing else.
- A custom bar that changes where a tab goes. Emit `tabPress`, respect a
  prevented default, then navigate — the navigator's own order.

## Always

- Spread a style from `type` rather than setting size, family, or tracking by hand.
- Use `space`, `inset`, `stack`, and `radius`. Page gutter (`inset.screen`)
  never pads a field or compact option. Sheets use `stack.group`, pages use
  `stack.section`. If the design needs a value that is not in the scale, change
  the scale deliberately and write down why.
- Check both schemes. Dark mode is a warm charcoal, not an inversion.
- Keep tappable areas at `HIT_TARGET` or give them `hitSlop`, on every platform.
- Check a narrow phone and a wide browser window. Resize the window: layout
  that reads a stale size looks right until it moves.
- Pass `inTabs` to `Screen` from a screen inside `(tabs)`, and only from there.
  A bottom tab bar owns the bottom inset; a wide left rail does not.
- Pass `inSheet` to `Screen` from a route presented as `modal`, and only from
  there. The sheet's card already starts below the status bar.
- Pad safe-area insets from `useSafeAreaInsets`. `SafeAreaView` reads its own
  position on screen and reports nothing for the top inside a `fullScreenModal`.
- Give every gesture a keyboard or pointer equivalent. A mouse has no thumb.
- Use `ChoiceRow` for selectable lists. Selection is a brass left rule and
  quiet surface shift, never a filled pill cloud.
- Render everything below a watch's price from `ListingDetails`. The deck card
  and the listing route are two frames on one block, and the frame passes in its
  own buttons.
- Scroll inside a swipe card with React Native's `ScrollView`. Gesture
  Handler's takes the whole touch on web and the card stops moving. Keep
  `activeOffsetX` and `failOffsetY` on the pan so the two axes stay separate.

## When the rules do not cover it

Decide, build it, and add the rule to `docs/DESIGN.md` and `src/lib/design.ts`
in the same change. An undocumented one-off becomes the thing the next screen
copies.
